**Lemma 4.3 (D2 extraction without a registry or image sidecar).** For every
$h\in\Omega_2$, finite word operations on its M-body and the fixed public
code extract

$$
\bigl(\operatorname{code}(u),J_0(h),J_1(h),A(h),n(h)\bigr).
\tag{PVC.6}
$$

$J_0$ is old variable ingress before Install, $J_1$ installed external
ingress, $A=\bot$ before Install and otherwise the actual number of completed
old frames at activation, and $n$ the absolute receipt count. The occupied
variable bit occurs exactly once in its appropriate reservoir.

Proof. Recover $u$ from the authentic no-update rows/backing by the original
preorder acquisition, using its original preparation/fence rather than a
later private packet. This is SSA Proposition 2.1 and CSA Lemma 5.3's
acquisition case. Count existing meter receipts to obtain $n$; the finite
serialized meter end is part of this old body.
Only the basic selected structures are used here; the later cover/package
fold of Definition 4.2 is not a premise of extraction or replay.

Before activation AIF Theorem 4.2 gives old written ingress plus its unique
occupied bit, $A=\bot$ and empty $J_1$. After the Install CTL, including
before the first manifest bit, the installing frontier distinguishes that
choice; all earlier old frames are complete. Count those complete frames
to obtain $A$, retaining their full ordered bits as $J_0$. Fixed code and
capture inputs do not enter either variable reservoir. During head saves,
asset copying and manifest construction these old complete bits remain
unchanged. Once frozen, their manifest-prefix copy identifies exactly
the same $J_0,A$, excluding later source-clone extensions on old ports.

For installed ingress use its immutable 38 blocks and current reader
frontier. Header IN/EX/WR and length/payload IN/EX/WR preserve latch 6 until
the corresponding WR; tests use latch 5. Between IN and WR append that
one bit to the written prefix. At and after WR it is in the prefix and
the optional field is empty. Source-clone RD(38), imports and serializers
consume no external input. This includes every Convert identifier,
destination choice and all partial unary fields. Registry appends after
ACK, graph/word operations and final return have no IN at all. Thus none
creates a missing external-choice coordinate. Lists, counters and tests
are the finite scans of Definitions 2.1 and 4.2. ∎

